msgid "It was small, and the high walls made it feel more secluded than it perhaps was."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 60b68804aa429613293e29a1665853e3
msgctxt "speaker:Guard"
msgid "It was smart not to make a fire."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 89dc4de2766ac9088a27ffdc8ac4829b
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It was smart of you to gather what information we have available to us. It can't ever hurt."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 62620a1f26509daaa1abd98d9aeb1907
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was smarter to keep going, she knew that."
msgstr ""

#. uid: d0d934891541ac408c9c47ed08e77927
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was smarter to keep watch..."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 9f2cb2c63117777db65313bad3706d13
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was so simple, it barely counted as a spell. But it was enough."
msgstr ""

#. uid: afa0fb522c755e8ffb5af165c261c0fa
msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "It was some other sorry bastard five months ago, and it will be another sorry bastard five months from now."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 1b98e28f3ecdd0880bd10bf2c2f1c9e3
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was some six years, and by now mother to three children, when Sarah watched her husband return one last time."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 4d998196f61196446113e11c0c28cd3d
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was something she looked forward to with almost mad desperation."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 43a93805c615fcb59e504cb5dd15ccd4
msgctxt "speaker:Nathan"
msgid "It was something short...I think."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 2af0583f74bca4881408bbd5c774610e
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was something that was entirely normal. Something that he deserved."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 86dc75b3fcb56b78378717324320139b
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was still early in the morning when they were ready to depart."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 94ff96f5d4bf2c90e27848742420df90
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was still hard for Sarah to adapt to the fact that now, all these rules seemed to fall away."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 3ba4600aab79507ea55ee77da882f2c0
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was still hard for her to imagine they had actually survived their ordeal."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 2296e523ea9da8c3ba318c7d967d7219
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was still night. How long had she been out for?"
msgstr ""

#. uid: 667159a3968557a2365b16056a074065
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was still odd to her that this great seat of power, the center of her nation, was at night often empty."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 14233b3084ef5d859c8b71e1022a0f67
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was still strange to her to consider that she had an army of her own."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 9a392fb3b9eb47edc6262177abd06ccb
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was still the same girl, and yet everything about her looked different."
msgstr ""

#. uid: d3c1eef2ff0ac465b6df2f552b224b33
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was still there, but it had begun to lessen. To transform into something else, or perhaps begin a process of transformation."
msgstr ""

#. uid: e6570d11cbce4433587841a4edfe6f05
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was strange how for a man his size, he could be so delicate."
msgstr ""

#. uid: fd672ec0097b3b1741130d08d84a0ae1
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was strange how the enormous thing seemed to exist in the background of the city."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 6ef98ba57277484c0063497f3e06bf75
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was strange to Sarah. Lady Carolyn was the one who was standing entirely naked, and yet, Sarah was the one who felt embarassed."
msgstr ""

#. uid: c76db9894abaacf96b1e3aaaa2160fd8
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was strange to her how something that had once been so normal now sounded wrong to her."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 2a18564a6306e87e14b16926318eb5a1
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was strange to once again just have a conversation with someone."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 4b316a455c7b359bc9e7c811fef28b89
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was strange walking here, in such relative calm, when she knew that just an ocean away, a horde of demons roamed free."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 6a3c493e93690299e02c70c689a50484
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was strangely peaceful."
msgstr ""

#. uid: e068fe0b8c431ca1423e7025ebb21e8c
msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "It was strategy. Same reason I defeated them."
msgstr ""

#. uid: b96d8b1c6f73670f250bd638883bd5cb
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was stunning."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 147f6bc37007e299f9745fc30677a792
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It was stupid, but my friend he...convinced me."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 8aa508abcb601ded5dce3bcfa7e3014f
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was subtle, easy to miss if she didn't know what to look for."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 8c064fa8fc0d0eabbafea3fc17d12711
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was subtle, the way in which people turned away from him, guarding their wallets with their bodies, or simply moving away entirely."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 23c8fe4af3663269009ca94fa495c199
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was such, sitting and waiting, that Sarah was finally approached by one of the soldiers that worked as a messenger."
msgstr ""

#. uid: ee2143c38ed447d88d5b46c9797cd40b
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was suicide."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 34e0357f166be82f3edfe51268d6d153
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was tempting to believe how simple a life she could have here."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 616767fa1e8636fe4faaf39fa070c43a
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was that belief that made it possible for her to debase herself in front of the old man."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 0eb8331fab7db09d78ec1517e4b3fe7d
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was that fact which had wounded her most."
msgstr ""

#. uid: b88810c8e5c8457e4ee61a55b8558055
msgctxt "speaker:Guard Captain"
msgid "It was that fucking lowlife partner of yours. He got you all twisted and on the wrong path."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 9b497cca666c50e35c6f731786e98034
msgctxt "speaker:Hassar"
msgid "It was that lack of strength that caused your downfall, and that has brought you to me."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 68d0e496a080050f3da4ea0873836aad
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the Khan that answered."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 8268751f9efd78701c920263ec72b5c0
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the Tribesmen that had ran out of steam."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 1105ae32aa2e57808116936cb119291a
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the best pain they had ever felt."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 935211170506cc2afcd9a9940874cda0
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the citizens of Calshure that lived, that they hated the most. Their weakness."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 1dfd42ccbd47cc99c50ee920de21e13a
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the exact sigil of her House."
msgstr ""

#. uid: a0dce7b1011db33acf920023d04acd87
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the first thing on her agenda. And then tomorrow the council meeting."
msgstr ""

#. uid: dc578c09672cc72269f6a3f7be87a3ca
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the first thing she noticed, how his blade was clean and maintained, their daggers stained in rust. It said everything."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 40f45d92591bbb332ea2a911a62c1421
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the former that only ever concerned the nation's nobility, whereas the latter was of a second concern."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 1461289ae206ea4f5eef22f0ac66834a
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the kind of burden that had rested on her shoulders for so long that she had almost forgotten it."
msgstr ""

#. uid: b5e4159e9601c3ab30d2e5830fd6a4b3
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the kind that sank into your bones, like pain in a tooth."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 6bf0319f75c8c1d070b66e7cfa8fc81c
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the latter part that had surprised her the most."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 132eb0450c9a93d876c11a3a751c8928
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the most beautiful thing she had ever seen in her life. The most beautiful thing she would ever see in her life."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 0af58f10d29fb4ee4f2f02fb2860edd6
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the most dangerous out of all that he had offered. But at the same time, Sarah had found it the most appealing."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 1c0feaba3de3632a05a6d924ce31a7fc
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the next night when what had been made official in her heart, would now be etched unto her skin."
msgstr ""

#. uid: dd57161fb3ef78c3c0cc0eb64755c6bb
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the only thing she could think about."
msgstr ""

#. uid: b05cf6c93db0f613d69a05f0677e4636
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the prelude of her life, the castle, the wealth, the unearned titles...that was undeserved."
msgstr ""

#. uid: d26490e9991a9ad7309c1edbea7e81d9
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the silence. The city had gone silent."
msgstr ""

#. uid: e9fff44c0d481df4a3ed2fb8eb69a251
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the size of the thing, she concluded."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 73ce739ff05816cba2f28379f1ee9fb8
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the slow tragedy of an empire that did not fall in one day, but instead, seemed to have been falling for centuries."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 7780a0c89031c3f21e869a17458ec4dc
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the smile that made Sarah recognize her, even underneath the mask."
msgstr ""

#. uid: ffea60d20077128f149a82d2c2bf5f53
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the some colour as the goblin poison."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 43a6ac52a4bd28cd8b09a3d01d17c17e
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the spirit, unmistakably, only larger."
msgstr ""

#. uid: ba0a5399bb6b9f6380ec0535528cbd6d
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the thing they had risked their lives for."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 8182f1b29bd469b8badd8332ff34ac58
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the truth, but Sarah also knew it didn't really matter."
msgstr ""

#. uid: e6fb6c1961358aa8bbdaf3facd73fcea
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the truth, she'd never slept with a woman before."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 21c806afd86289f25168826cf2d7e667
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the truth, she'd slept with Kate."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 51bac5722df682838a89fd9402bcf64d
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the truth."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 3d462dd0ea0c328fc5a738a032d3c9fb
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the very first town large enough for them to rest in."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 3ed16d51d1e8b4d2a19e9a80b13bbbf1
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was the whores and easy women in every port that he truly loved. Her ruined body would mean nothing to him."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 9d151fe82779fa0c6b29d9845f6d718c
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was then perhaps no surprise they had failed to prepare as well as they could have."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 816dd697470d5f8ccece22831c175f1b
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was thick, heavy, sticky. As if he hadn't been released in a long time."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 017708c9241084b673e508b7fffd4dc8
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was this arrogance that had brought Sarah and Xan to the city."
msgstr ""

#. uid: e404e03368e92e73d950aba246f9cce5
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was this carefully orchestrated balance that allowed the city to remain independent."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 784ffdc4b99ffcaa202e20542c1ac307
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was this house."
msgstr ""

#. uid: d364a4dd746dbc09d9202ddf9e56259c
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was this last fact that caused the ship to unkowingly become less nimble."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 68bc34bf3e046ccbf235fffad8bdf8ab
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was this resentment that Marion had played into."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 662f8a3cff8af5382675caa642536d6d
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was this, or the whip, and Sarah much preferred this."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 3d4ef12e154ac59d088f4b2eabe5c470
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was to be expected, she realized as she kept cooking."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 282ff8f4260f3562a1a98ed45bdd8f6a
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was to be expected."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 2e697f620e4167b6486027ad1be9f3c3
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was too much to keep in."
msgstr ""

#. uid: cad0f05b571db43b81fd95eef98aa5e2
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was too much."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 8a5f26eedd7e38ebbe59a56094a93cba
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was too tempting to refuse."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 0081064fe2f6df12f45aad8a9a0692cd
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was true that Varga, besides his tactical skill, was also a skilled enough warrior."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 493cc41d19c58e4ec264dd460ddc637a
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was true that if they were to form a unified army, each nation would have to supply soldiers."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 98386dae6704ed8b6f8c13972ed10e1b
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was true that she was frightened of him, but that feeling seemed to fade with every moment."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 1ffef6a850b9dba69712202ef3cd4396
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was true that what he told her was different from what she had imagined, and yet, she still doubted that the story was as nice as he led on."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 1686ce0462a6e2660d93e99a564bfbdd
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was true what he said. Most everyone on the council hailed from nobility, Varga was the rare exception."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 0adf56a8ac204aeb17f6373e018dfc48
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was true when they had left, perhaps. But a lot had changed since then, and Sarah could no longer look at Nick the same way."
msgstr ""

#. uid: b160439140b453bc788a244560950a73
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was true, Sarah couldn't deny that."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 8f256cb8e66e1c3a0224483a955eb581
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was true, Sarah remembered. The land on the western side of the capital ran far lower, almost like a valley. They would literally be fighting uphill."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 82943f8acf8888b40182659676840845
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was true, but Sarah had grown tired. She had a war to fight and win, and she would not do it from this place."
msgstr ""

#. uid: e90942faeeeb91a84e2e98843a28f6d2
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was true, but still she had decided on the spirit."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 993504d9661df8943599ddafab865a2d
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was true, whether she wanted to admit it or not."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 43ee03826d203469ec6b622f6160fdba
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was true. All those years ago, he had only ever used her mouth."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 6abf885cdf135f712f651597ecd89e77
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was true. Rosanna and Medini, kept apart by the two nations that laid between them, had rarely ever seen direct conflict."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 9becc921a1033317b0425b284848aeae
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was ugly business, but it was the business of peace."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 894c0e895046301a2e4e9e5531f46226
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was under these circumstances that they came upon the one thing that broke through the monotonous environment of the forest."
msgstr ""

#. uid: ecaf605e79c12c19aac7a879772adec9
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was under this same set of unclear circumstances that Sarah now found herself in the great palace of the city of Bagrad."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 1fd738d69086a5d63582f683f58fe576
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "It was unfair that you never had that certainty about me. Ooh Sarah, if I could make this up to you, I would."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 065764bd69a3dda600d05b49cab8e8fe
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was vast, as all rooms in this Estate appeared to be, but compared to the great hall it felt smaller. Private."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 6a6893b4a82290313eb14a213f316f06
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was vile enough to be subjected to their leering eyes."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 6690f76dffe07956bfda650ad6b38aad
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was warmer here in the tent, but not by much."
msgstr ""

#. uid: c3874f1993ec62d9e7ef9033279e74eb
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was well kept, but plain. The type of home one might expect of a Huntsman in a town out nowhere."
msgstr ""

#. uid: be1b92d9313bf69a381711686a53fdc6
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was what Hassar had wanted to avoid, and exactly what Thomas had hoped for. Hassar's cavalry drove straight into a fortified front line, lined with pikes designed to counter the cavalry charge."
msgstr ""

#. uid: d54a98f789d8a4d8b1a8aa6bffe6578e
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was what he wanted to hear, as much as it was the truth."
msgstr ""

#. uid: f961bac0fcb4233ff9857f238c3c8ae0
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was what she had wanted, and yet, she still found herself doubting, for a brief moment."
msgstr ""

#. uid: ce61c11943b809edd0a863d38c1ce69d
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was with good spirits that their wagon turned further along the road, coming upon the first sign of human life, outside of the old road itself, that Sarah had seen for days."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 93f6d280a6ad0a29efd2611d3d73c8d2
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was with these thoughts, endlessly repeating in her mind, that Sarah eventually found herself back in to harbor."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 2cec28d42957c4c7469a95fbb1f42028
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was worth it."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 11530b2fdf28aec7d3423420003f03fb
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was would be at least several hours before she finally managed to get out from under the creature and find it a place to live."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 0ab6c0ec55e9e60881870bd7ffb2e194
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was wrong...wrong for her to see this...and yet, for it, all the more arousing."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 3b6bd122d71749591dae71d197f8d106
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It was you...and your ship...on the night that I..."
msgstr ""

#. uid: cf50eb6bbe4b21ba69ae785c408ca671
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It was. I mean, I did have fun."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 809693933a01d1f358a42dd8b4aff2ae
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "It was..."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 1d0bfcf58e4e7588e6a4ff3014f5aebb
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It wasn't a day for idle chatter."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 204be1b34b6a80caf0599af450bd59c5
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It wasn't an overt sadness, but rather a sort of omnipresent depression. As if the very bricks in the wall ached with tiredness."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 713866a0910a1d77d050fc2fa9ba513b
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It wasn't anything special, but in that moment, it was one of the best sleeps she ever had."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 9bfabcf7997c255c7635eda382de61d5
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It wasn't as easy as she imagined. Each time, more words or thoughts slipped in between."
msgstr ""

#. uid: b53feadccc71b3d2655fa5192d468830
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It wasn't coming from the city...but."
msgstr ""

#. uid: df90d85b840f4823497bf0cf803055ae
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It wasn't easy."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 7c6b55106c8ba7ca2451337323a84b64
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It wasn't even a white lie, she'd really been incredible."
msgstr ""

#. uid: e4e7b8a3621d1c80e11ff60e1c5655f6
msgctxt "speaker:Nickolas"
msgid "It wasn't fair of me to be. You've lived your own life, and had to survive your own way."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 7e4c5593be28f41df61bb344e0e070ed
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It wasn't fair, but then again, Sarah rationalized, Belmont had never pretended that their arrangement would be fair."
msgstr ""

#. uid: e5354634aa41cbe8e13b293dca0d0bda
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It wasn't glory, that much she knew."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 6e2a722dcd443878e3c4c2d58700e7b3
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It wasn't hard for Sarah to tell his intentions."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 32357eacf96da1ea21984e9ce3e85d01
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It wasn't her fault, quite the opposite. Sarah blamed herself more than anything."
msgstr ""

#. uid: c8482db23d13c648bb85bc8c88ede888
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It wasn't her job to fight his battles."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 7b1faffc2169e75a77210cc555654427
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It wasn't her place to tell Lily how to run her own noble House, but still she hoped she was partially joking."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 38ede518b0d8f9bda5a335d9ab6d7b76
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It wasn't his fault, quite the opposite. Sarah blamed herself more than anything."
msgstr ""

#. uid: f5d8cff9ad1c0040bf0b2d4627e8955d
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It wasn't ideal, but it was as close of a chance they had of averting disaster."
msgstr ""

#. uid: ca8ab96f22b42786b993d8ce3bedd7d6
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It wasn't just amusement that it was getting from this."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 4639cc6f3052d749920614f0965f7ec0
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It wasn't just the loud noises from before, but also softer ones, scratching."
msgstr ""

#. uid: 84b5704da00f3698ccdf2e50d59cf41d
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It wasn't like before. Nick wasn't in the room next over, he was right here. She didn't need to spare his feelings by curbing her own desires."
msgstr ""

